WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.097
You do not need to memorize the entire NumPy API.

00:00:04.097 --> 00:00:15.297
For analytics and introductory data science, focus on the core patterns that you are likely to reuse: creating arrays,

00:00:15.297 --> 00:00:22.827
checking shape and data type, performing vectorized calculations, selecting and filtering values, understanding axes,

00:00:22.827 --> 00:00:31.162
reshaping data, using broadcasting, generating random values, and calculating descriptive statistics.

00:00:31.744 --> 00:00:37.161
You should also understand missing numerical values, copies versus views,

00:00:37.161 --> 00:00:43.881
and how arrays connect to machine learning mathematics such as standardization and dot products.

00:00:43.881 --> 00:00:50.726
If you can explain these ideas and use them in small problems, you have a strong foundation for the next stage of the

00:00:50.726 --> 00:00:51.777
course.
